2026-11-01 re-PUBLISHed (empty law titles): 5 law title(s) that were empty are now the law's ementa. The title reader (titles.ementa) keeps the old full-stop reading first and otherwise reads the layouts it missed: no full stop before the enacting formula, the formula in other forms ('O Presidente da República', 'PRESIDENTE DA REPÚBLICA', 'OS MINISTROS DA MARINHA ...', 'O Congresso Nacional decreta'), page navigation and links between the ementa and the formula, ementas longer than the old window, and an ementa a later act rewrote (the enacted wording is the title). Every law now has the same title in every part where any part had one empty. Installed = the previous file with only these law fields changed (fresh parse of every part with the final code: no other law differs, apart from known pre-existing drift); acts, versions and decisions unchanged. Per-part checks re-run before/after: identical output. Installed sha256 bd00a678. Merged scratch build with every installed part: 211 acts, 3323 versions, 2435 commits, check.py 0 mismatches, 0 trailer errors, --compare identical, audit_push clean on main and futuro.
